1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,401
Rejection at the zone: what to
look for when price gets there.

2
00:00:03,601 --> 00:00:07,703
Price has reached the zone. The
first touch isn't the entry:

3
00:00:07,703 --> 00:00:09,138
wait for a rejection.

4
00:00:09,138 --> 00:00:12,898
You can spot it on M15, or
drop to M5 to see it sooner.

5
00:00:13,098 --> 00:00:16,466
A pin bar: a long wick into
the zone and a small body.

6
00:00:16,466 --> 00:00:19,835
Sellers pushed in, and buyers
pushed price right back.

7
00:00:20,035 --> 00:00:21,301
An engulfing candle:

8
00:00:21,301 --> 00:00:25,227
its body fully covers the one
before, in the zone's direction.

9
00:00:25,227 --> 00:00:26,936
Control just changed hands.

10
00:00:27,136 --> 00:00:28,204
A liquidity sweep:

11
00:00:28,204 --> 00:00:33,541
price breaks a recent low inside the zone,
takes the stops below it, and snaps right back.

12
00:00:33,541 --> 00:00:35,973
What looked like a breakdown was a sweep.

13
00:00:36,173 --> 00:00:37,014
A false break:

14
00:00:37,014 --> 00:00:41,161
price pushes out of the zone, but
the candle body closes back inside.

15
00:00:41,161 --> 00:00:44,166
The break didn't hold, and
that's a rejection too.

16
00:00:44,366 --> 00:00:46,704
A new Fair Value Gap or Order Block:

17
00:00:46,704 --> 00:00:52,225
after the turn, price moves away fast and
leaves one behind, in the zone's direction.

18
00:00:52,225 --> 00:00:53,719
Buyers are stepping in.

19
00:00:53,919 --> 00:00:57,233
These are the most common,
but not the only ones.

20
00:00:57,383 --> 00:01:02,311
A double bottom: price tests the zone,
bounces, and comes back for a second test.

21
00:01:02,483 --> 00:01:07,689
The second low holds at or above the first.
Sellers tried twice and couldn't push lower.

22
00:01:08,183 --> 00:01:12,407
A morning star: a strong bearish
candle, then a small one that hesitates,

23
00:01:12,403 --> 00:01:16,286
then a strong bullish candle that
closes past the middle of the first.

24
00:01:16,433 --> 00:01:17,799
Momentum just turned.

25
00:01:18,333 --> 00:01:23,219
A break of structure on M5: on the way
down, price keeps making lower highs.

26
00:01:23,333 --> 00:01:27,024
When it breaks above the last one,
the drop on that timeframe is over.

27
00:01:27,633 --> 00:01:31,077
Any of them, on M15 or M5,
means price is reacting.

28
00:01:31,277 --> 00:01:33,863
And if price doesn't react? Don't chase it.

29
00:01:33,863 --> 00:01:36,570
Let the zone go and wait for the next report.

30
00:01:36,570 --> 00:01:39,638
A missed trade costs you
nothing. A forced one can.

31
00:01:39,838 --> 00:01:41,440
Let price show its hand.

